  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7b8860589b05b4642ab42b24201a782d, type: 3}
  m_Name: Book_MeatThatKeeps
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GrandmasHouse::GrandmasHouse.Data.NoteData
  kind: 3
  title: Meat That Keeps
  recipe: {fileID: 0}
  body: 
  marginNote: 
  pages:
  - 'Fresh meat keeps a day or two, and you must never eat it raw. Cook it in the
    pot, or put it by: smoked or salted, it will see you through to spring.'
  - 'The smokehouse


    Hang the meat on the hooks and light a fire underneath.
    A fire burns most of a night and then dies down, so light it again if the meat
    isn''t done. It wants about sixteen hours of smoke in all.


    Smoked meat
    keeps for weeks, and you can eat it as it is.'
  - 'The salt box


    The box down in the cellar is for salting meat. Pour plenty
    of salt in first, then pack the meat into it. Give it three days. Each piece
    uses up a scoop of salt, so keep the box topped up.


    Salted meat keeps longer
    than anything.'
  mentions: []
